--- the score ---
score           : demo at 8000 Hz, 0 events
event (buffer)  : buffer buffer 4000 at 0 for 0.4
event (file)    : file drums.wav
call            : call blip ; a bare function is called with the duration: (dur)
instrument      : synth ping ((freq 660))
event-at        : a stereo buffer at azimuth 45 elevation 10
event-gain! ... : gain 0.8 ; moved to 1.4 for 0.25 at -30
score-duration  : 2.3 s; event-end of the last: 2.3
score demo : 6 events, 2.3 s at 8000 Hz
   0 0.4 buffer buffer 4000 
   0.5 0.3 file drums.wav 
   1 0.2 call call blip 
   1.4 0.25 call call blip @-30,0
   1.6 0.3 synth synth ping 
   2 0.3 buffer buffer x2 @45,10

--- rendering ---
render-event    : 1 channel of 3200 samples (cut to the duration, faded at the end)
fit-duration    : 100 (shorter sounds are left alone)
layout-channels : mono 1 stereo 2 binaural 2 ambi 2 9 ring of 6 6 8 channels 8
place           : a mono sound at the left, stereo levels (0.707 0)
score-render    : 2 channels, 23200 samples
render: the mix peaked at 1.23 and was scaled to 0.98
render          : written to /tmp/musil_reference_score.wav

--- the roll ---
score-rows      : (files buffers synths calls)
score-roll      : a figure with 6 bars in 4 rows
event-lanes     : (0 1 0) (overlapping events get lanes)
display         : (display s) shows the roll: staves, note heads and duration lines; Play from the cursor, a double-click plays an event

--- transformations ---
score-shift!    : the first event now at 1
score-scale!    : ... and at 0.5 for 0.2
score-select    : 2 calls
score-sort!     : first at 0.5
score-remove!   : 5 events left
score-merge     : 10 events in the merged score

--- database ---
db-load         : 32 entries; spectrum features, 1024 coefficients; root microsol
db-instruments  : (Ob Hn Vn Vc)
db-techniques   : (ord)  db-dynamics: (mf ff)  db-pitches: 9
db-query        : 8 mf violin sounds; 1 exact
db-range        : violin (60 67) =  C4 to G4
an entry        : Vn ord C#4 mf 4c midi 61
db-features     : 1024 values
db-path         : Vn-ord-C#4-mf-4c.wav ; db-available? 1
pitch->midi     : 60 75 58  midi->pitch: D#5
note            : Vn C4 mf shift 0 ; Vn B4 mf uses G4 shifted 4
note-path       : Vn-ord-C4-mf-4c.wav  note-duration: 7.35 s
score-rows      : notes by instrument, orchestral order: (Ob Vn Vc)

--- elements ---
rhythm, beats   : (1 0.5 -0.5 1) lasts 3 s; at 120 bpm: (0.5 0.25 -0.25 0.5)
chord           : Vn chord C4 E4 G4
notes           : ((0 0.25 C4) (0.25 0.5 D4) (0.75 0.25 E4)) (the rhythm repeats under the line)
chords          : 2 chord events
texture         : 6 notes: one line at two speeds, the faster repeating
pivots          : (D4 D4 D4 A#4 F#4 F4) (two lines wandering around C4 and G4)
chordinterp     : ((C4 E4 G4) (C#4 F4 G#4) (D4 F4 A4))
transpose, invert, scale-pitches: (62 nil 66) (60 56) (62 64 65 67 69 71 72 74)
more elements   : score-tempo!/add-beats!, fragment-gain/dynamics/articulate/thin/density/place/snap, chord-voicing, pitch-field, rotate/retrograde/cycle/interleave, harmonic-series, pitches-from-spectrum, rhythm-from-pattern/augment/diminish, tuplet, polyrhythm, walk, texture-staggered, arpeggio, chordinterp-ease/-sets, texture-on-chords/-pivots, orchestrate-line, score-map!, score-instrument (algorithmic_comp.mu uses them)
fragments       : duration 1 ; shifted (2 2.25 2.75) ; scaled (0 0.5 1.5) ; repeated 9 ; until 2.6 s: 8
add!            : 3 events placed; 3 more at the left
fragment->score : inner with 3 events
a score inside  : kind score for 1.6 s (0 = its whole length); rendered 185220 samples; a score cannot contain itself

--- midi, granular orchestration ---
midi-read       : 4 notes in (Piano Bass) , 1.75 s
midi->fragment  : 4 events; midi->score: an instrument per channel; velocity->dynamics f
env, env-at     : (2.25 3.5) (ranges interpolated; sets crossfaded by chance)
orchestra       : 5 players, (Ob Hn Vn Vc) ; an ossia Vn|Vc, a paired (Vn Vc)
orchestrate-granular: 1 segment, 2 solutions; the best connection has 26 events; connect! places one
playability     : a note is a sample the player's instrument has (player-styles, player-pitches, db-pitches-at); 'dynamics-strict makes the dynamics a constraint too; what no player can play is reported and left out
report          : 21 events due, 26 notes, 1 skipped with every able player busy, 0 unplayable, 25 at another dynamics; a line per player (notes, busy fraction, seat); granulation-report prints it
just-cents      : -31 cents, the 7th partial of C2 (a 'harmonic granulator with 'just 1 tunes its partials so); a signed 'leap (list -2 -1) is a descending line
the players     : 'seat (an ossia player keeps its instrument), 'leap (steps from its last pitch), 'inertia (keeps its technique), 'weight and 'tilt (where in the band), 'spread (a group's attack scattered), 'duration-law ('log or an exponent), 'group-density (a rate per group), 'balance (dB per instrument or family: 0.501 for the Hn)
continue, start : two granulators on one orchestra, overlapping, book the same people once; score-validate: playable (a player of its own for every note, at a recorded pitch); peak ((Hn 1) (Vc 1) (Ob 1) (Vn 1)) ; validation-print prints it; orchestra-rest! clears the state
db-index!       : 4 instruments indexed once (what note draws from); db-candidates, db-range-available, db-techniques-of (ord)

--- morphological ---
target-analyse  : 2.6 s, 111 frames; curves: density (flux peaks a second), centroid, spread, low, loudness; 1 flux peaks
target-envelopes: the granulator's parameters from the curves: (density dynamics register)
target-peaks    : the pitches the notes may take, at 1 s: (C4 C6 C5 C7 A#6 E7)
orchestrate-morphological: 1 notes with cents, e.g. Vc C4 f 15 cents; a matching pursuit at every event (target-notes), each note as long as the target keeps its sound (atom-persistence), no segmentation

--- queries, db-gen, playing ---
db-query (lists): 16 string sounds, mf or ff
db-grep         : 2 violin C4 and C#4 (a regular expression on the file name)
db-find         : 2 cello C's (a substring)
db-between      : 5 violin sounds between C4 and E4
db-nearest      : (Vn-ord-C#4-mf-4c.wav Hn-ord-C#4-mf.wav Vc-ord-C#4-mf-1c.wav) (closest features)
db-available    : 32 sounds on disk; db-instruments-available: (Ob Hn Vn Vc)
db-gen          : 32 sounds analysed into /tmp/musil_reference_gen.db (mfcc, 13); db-make generates and loads
play-score      : (play-score s gain) renders the score, puts it in the concert hall (score-reverb!) and plays it; (play-score-from s gain from) from a time
score-play-now  : starts and returns (the roll's Play); stop-score stops; playhead reads the cursor
rendered /tmp/musil_reference_hall.wav (in the hall)
render-hall     : 2 channels in the hall, to a file (the roll's Render...)
score-schedule  : the live way, every event on the clock (synths compiled, no hall); returns the synths to free
db-merge        : 64 entries out of two databases (or (db-load (list "a.db" "b.db")))
